PART 4: CONTROLLED TEXTAREA
================================================================================

A controlled textarea uses essentially the same pattern as a controlled
text input.


File:

src/components/ControlledTextarea.jsx


import { useState } from 'react'
import './ControlledTextarea.css'


export default function ControlledTextarea() {

  const [message, setMessage] =
    useState('')


  const handleChange = (event) => {

    setMessage(
      event.target.value
    )
  }


  const wordCount =
    message
      .trim()
      .split(/\s+/)
      .filter(Boolean)
      .length


  return (
    <div className="controlled-textarea-container">

      <h1>
        Controlled Textarea
      </h1>


      <div className="form-group">

        <label htmlFor="message">
          Message:
        </label>


        <textarea
          id="message"
          value={message}
          onChange={handleChange}
          placeholder="Enter your message"
          rows={5}
          className="form-textarea"
        />

      </div>


      <div className="display-section">

        <h3>
          Current Value:
        </h3>


        <p>

          Message:
          {' '}

          <strong>
            {message || '(empty)'}
          </strong>

        </p>


        <p>

          Length:
          {' '}

          <strong>
            {message.length}
          </strong>
          {' '}
          characters

        </p>


        <p>

          Words:
          {' '}

          <strong>
            {wordCount}
          </strong>

        </p>

      </div>

    </div>
  )
}


================================================================================
TEXTAREA PATTERN
================================================================================

STATE:

const [message, setMessage] =
  useState('')


VALUE:

value={message}


CHANGE:

onChange={(event) =>
  setMessage(
    event.target.value
  )
}


================================================================================
IMPORTANT REACT TEXTAREA DIFFERENCE
================================================================================

In plain HTML you may see:

<textarea>
  Initial text
</textarea>


For a controlled React textarea, use:

<textarea
  value={message}
  onChange={handleChange}
/>


The value prop controls the textarea content.


================================================================================
WORD COUNT
================================================================================

A more robust basic word count is:

const wordCount =
  message
    .trim()
    .split(/\s+/)
    .filter(Boolean)
    .length


This handles multiple spaces and line breaks better than:

message.split(' ')


