PART 9: CONTROLLED ELEMENTS COMPARISON
================================================================================

+---------------------+-------------------+----------------------+----------------+
| ELEMENT             | CONTROL PROP      | EVENT DATA           | EXAMPLE        |
+---------------------+-------------------+----------------------+----------------+
| Text Input          | value             | target.value         | "John"         |
| Email Input         | value             | target.value         | "a@b.com"      |
| Password Input      | value             | target.value         | text string    |
| Number Input        | value             | target.value         | "42"           |
| Textarea            | value             | target.value         | "Hello"        |
| Select              | value             | target.value         | "india"        |
| Checkbox            | checked           | target.checked       | true           |
| Radio               | checked           | target.value         | "option-a"     |
| Range               | value             | target.value         | "50"           |
| Date                | value             | target.value         | "2026-11-01"   |
+---------------------+-------------------+----------------------+----------------+


================================================================================
IMPORTANT DIFFERENCES
================================================================================

TEXT / EMAIL / TEXTAREA / SELECT:

value={state}


CHECKBOX:

checked={booleanState}


RADIO:

checked={
  state === optionValue
}


ALL:

onChange={handler}


================================================================================
IMPORTANT: NUMBER AND RANGE VALUES
================================================================================

Even when an input has:

type="number"

or:

type="range"


event.target.value is generally a string.


Example:

User enters:

42


event.target.value:

"42"


If application state should contain a number:

const amount =
  event.target.value === ''
    ? ''
    : Number(
        event.target.value
      )


================================================================================
IMPORTANT: FILE INPUT
================================================================================

File inputs are special.

Files are accessed through:

event.target.files


Example:

const file =
  event.target.files[0]


Do not treat:

<input type="file">

like a normal controlled text input.


================================================================================
PART 10: BENEFITS OF CONTROLLED ELEMENTS
================================================================================

BENEFIT 1: STATE-DRIVEN VALUE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

React state can represent the current form value.

Example:

const [name, setName] =
  useState('John')


Input:

<input
  value={name}
  onChange={...}
/>


Current UI value:

John


================================================================================
BENEFIT 2: REAL-TIME VALIDATION
================================================================================

Example:

const isTooShort =
  name.trim().length < 2


The UI can react immediately:

{name && isTooShort && (

  <p>
    Name is too short
  </p>

)}


