================================================================================
KEY TAKEAWAY
================================================================================

The controlled-element pattern is:

STATE
  ↓
value / checked
  ↓
FORM CONTROL
  ↓
USER INTERACTION
  ↓
onChange
  ↓
STATE UPDATE
  ↓
RENDER


For most text-like controls:

value={state}


For checkboxes:

checked={booleanState}


For radio buttons:

checked={
  state === optionValue
}


This creates a predictable state-driven form architecture while still allowing
you to choose uncontrolled inputs when native DOM form behavior better fits
the requirement.


